{
	title: 'Web chip row over the composer, with docked panels',
	spec: "The web status is a chip row over the composer. Wider than 40rem it is one row, 40px tall on touch screens and 32px with a fine pointer. Up to 40rem (phones) it has two lines, so the activity, model and cwd read in full: a 22px text line with the activity (tone dot and text), the context percent in heat and the session id at the right, over a 40px chip line with the cwd, model and spawn-budget chips, then the quota gauge and the session menu at the right. On each phone line the items start from nothing and grow to their whole text, the model first, so no line wraps. Each touch target reaches 44px, extending 4px up, never over the composer. The one row holds, left: the session id (when the row is at least 60ch), the cwd chip (truncated from the start, edged in the project color), the model chip (short name; the full name from 80ch; never truncated) and the spawn-budget chip: one thin 1px bar per subagent, no gaps or grouping, the number at 0 or above 8. Right: activity, context percent in heat, a quota gauge (one ring per usage window) below 80ch or each window's own ring and percent from 80ch, and the session menu. The cwd, budget, quota and menu chips open popover panels (popovertarget): a sheet across the app on touch screens, docked over its chip with a pointer, standing on the chip row so the composer and its draft stay in view and usable. A scrim above the row takes taps there and only closes the panel. The cwd panel lists the open tabs' directories in their colors plus a search-or-path field (/cd). The budget panel steps the budget and applies it on close; Escape keeps the old one. The quota panel lists each window's use and reset. The menu holds Find, Fork, Notifications, Session details and Close tab (in red). Escape closes a panel and never reaches the session; closing returns focus to its chip. The model chip opens the model picker. Mockup approved by the user 2026-11-23 (session 54-dot); the two phone lines replace its one phone row, which cut the cwd, model and activity to a few letters (user, 2026-11-23: keep the new design, bring back what the old row did better).",
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		"A popover's ::backdrop lets taps through (UA pointer-events: none), and showPopover inside beforetoggle throws; Panel.tsx therefore renders a plain .Scrim layer beside the popover.",
		'keys.ts pauses the session on Escape, so the panel stops keydown propagation; the Session details row hides the menu (flush) before showModal, so closing the dialog returns focus to the menu button.',
		"Panels hold a .field form, so tests and code select the composer's field as .Composer .field.",
		"The model name's quota fill (task 5f) is gone: the gauge replaced it, and status.quota and usageWindows.shortest were deleted.",
		"Restored invariant: on a 390px phone the activity, the model label and the cwd (up to the room left) read in full. Flex wrapping breaks lines by content size before shrinking, so the phone lines give the cwd, model and activity flex-basis 0 with max-width: max-content; the model's large flex-grow fills it first. A container query cannot style its own container, so the two lines hang on a 40rem media query, and the 80ch extras apply only past 40rem. Before/after screenshots at 320-1440px were checked in Chromium (session 54-lei)."
